      "message": "I assume that it\u0027s dropped when `VmInstance` is dropped. I assume that this CL doesn\u0027t change the behavior, but tell me if I did so by mistake.\n\nHere\u0027s my understanding: The boxed callback is sent to the `virtmgr` via `IVirtualMachine::registerCallback()`, and no more reference from the `libvmclient` side. In other words, the callback is dropped when `virtmgr` drops it.\n\n`virtmgr` keeps the callbacks in the `struct VmInstance` (we use the same name between `virtmgr`, and `libvmclient`), but it\u0027s returned back to the `libvmclient` when `IVirtualMachine::createVm()`. `virtmgr` doesn\u0027t seem to have strong reference to the created `IVirtualMachine` while its `struct State` only keeps weak reference.",
